{"ref": "Shulchan Arukh, Orach Chayim 672:1", "heRef": "שולחן ערוך, אורח חיים תער״ב:א׳", "sectionRef": "Shulchan Arukh, Orach Chayim 672", "indexTitle": "Shulchan Arukh, Orach Chayim", "heIndexTitle": "שולחן ערוך, אורח חיים", "categories": ["Halakhah", "Shulchan Arukh"], "next": "Shulchan Arukh, Orach Chayim 673", "sectionNames": ["Siman", "Seif"], "versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Maginei Eretz: Shulchan Aruch Orach Chaim, Lemberg, 1893", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002084080", "text": "<b>זמן הדלקת נר חנוכה. ובו ב סעיפים:</b><br><i data-commentator=\"Be'er HaGolah\" data-label=\"א\" data-order=\"1\"></i>אין מדליקין נר חנוכה קודם שתשקע החמה אלא <i data-commentator=\"Mishnah Berurah\" data-label=\"א\"></i>עם <i data-commentator=\"Magen Avraham\" data-order=\"1\"></i><i data-commentator=\"Ba'er Hetev\" data-order=\"1\"></i>סוף שקיעתה <i data-commentator=\"Eshel Avraham\" data-label=\"א\" data-order=\"1\"></i>לא מאחרים ולא מקדימים <i data-commentator=\"Be'er HaGolah\" data-label=\"ב\" data-order=\"2\"></i>ויש מי שאומר <i data-commentator=\"Mishnah Berurah\" data-label=\"ב\"></i>שאם הוא טרוד יכול להדליק <i data-commentator=\"Mishnah Berurah\" data-label=\"ג\"></i>מפלג המנחה ולמעלה <i data-commentator=\"Be'er HaGolah\" data-label=\"ג\" data-order=\"3\"></i>ובלבד <i data-commentator=\"Mishnah Berurah\" data-label=\"ד\"></i>שיתן בה שמן עד <i data-commentator=\"Ba'er Hetev\" data-order=\"2\"></i><i data-commentator=\"Sha'arei Teshuvah\" data-order=\"2\"></i>שתכלה רגל מן השוק:"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Sefaria Community Translation", "license": "CC0", "versionSource": "https://www.sefaria.org", "text": "Chanukah candles are not lit before sunset, but rather with the end of sunset, neither later nor before.  And there are those who say that if one is busy, it is permissible to light from Plag Hamincha and onward, as long one puts enough oil [so that the lamp will remain lit] until people stop passing through the marketplace."}], "available_versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Maginei Eretz: Shulchan Aruch Orach Chaim, Lemberg, 1893", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002084080"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Torat Emet 363", "license": "Public Domain", "versionSource": "http://www.toratemetfreeware.com/index.html?downloads"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Sefaria Community Translation", "license": "CC0", "versionSource": "https://www.sefaria.org"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "spanish", "actualLanguage": "es", "versionTitle": "Shulján Aruj, Oraj Jaim, trad. David Arias Weil [es]", "license": "unknown", "versionSource": "Own translation"}]}